# A finite conjugacy forest for Rudvalis Sylow involutions

The indices refer to the existing 16384 binary normal forms of the actual
Sylow candidate. Non-involutions have a point moved by their square. The
remaining nonidentity indices are either one of fifteen roots or conjugate
by an existing candidate generator to an index of smaller height.

The packed entries are untrusted witnesses; `FusionChecks` verifies every
entry by kernel reduction and `Fusion` proves their group-theoretic meaning.
No conjugacy-class table is assumed. The ATLAS source and left-action
convention are retained from `Sylow.Candidate` and `Model.PermutationData`.
-/

